Pale, hunched humanoids about three feet tall, bald and emaciated, with big floppy ears and white-blue skin. Their hands are stained with blood. The one the Party watched was pulling clothing and junk out of a boat tied up in the sewers, sniffing each piece and tossing it behind it. They screech when a fight turns against them and break away.

They do not bleed. A pick opened one through the chest and the flesh gave inward, with no wound's worth of blood. They fight with clubs and long leaping charges.

In the sewers beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] three of them served two taller men in reddish-blued robe-armor, who carried staffs, cast spells and seemed to direct them. The men bled like anyone, but one of them burst with a wave of dark energy when he was first wounded. The Party killed both men and two of the creatures; the third fled down a side passage.
